# A benchmark route for `scripts/play-linux.sh --bench example`: VICTORY_KEYS
# entries, one a line, and how long the run lasts. When the time is up the
# launcher ends the title cleanly (SIGTERM). Copy this file to make a route of
# your own and time it against your save: the seconds count from the moment the
# title starts reading input.
#
#   <seconds>:<key>          tap a key (0.2 s)
#   <from>-<to>:<key>        hold it from..to
#
# Keys: a letter or digit, Enter, Esc, Tab, Back, Up, Down, Left, Right.
# With a controller connected the keys also move the pad:
#   W/A/S/D the left stick, I/J/K/L the right stick (camera), Z/C the triggers.
#
# This one only gets past the start screens and stands still for a minute;
# it is a template, not a measured route.
duration=150
12:Enter
16:Enter
20:A
25:Enter
30:A
35:Enter
40:A
50:Enter
# Walk forward while turning slowly, as a world benchmark would.
90-120:W
95-105:L
